From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] twinapi.appcore: the diagnostic-data, education, kiosk and tailored-experience settings programs ask for

Microsoft Edge asks at start what the machine's diagnostic data level is,
whether it is a school's PC or a kiosk, and whether the user allows
tailored experiences (Windows.System.Profile.
PlatformDiagnosticsAndUsageDataSettings and EducationSettings,
Windows.System.UserProfile.AssignedAccessSettings and DiagnosticsSettings).
Wine had none of these classes ("RoGetActivationFactory Failed to find
library for ..." in David's Edge report, 2026-10-06). They now answer as a
machine with default settings does: diagnostic data "Required" (Basic),
or Group Policy's AllowTelemetry (Policies\Microsoft\Windows\
DataCollection) or the level set in Settings; not an education
environment; not a kiosk; tailored experiences only when the user turned
them on, no policy forbids them and optional (Full) data is sent. The
level changes only with policy, so CollectionLevelChanged never fires.

Test: test/privacysettings-gate.sh with test/privacysettings-probe.c
(mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_PRIVACY_SETTINGS).
